<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n211" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ab-sĭmĭlis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		ab, priv., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>unlike</i>, usually with a <i>neg.</i> and dat.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">falces non absimili formā muralium
					falcium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 3, 14, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b> With
				<i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(herba) neque absimilis bitumini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					6, 17, 2</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 33, 51, § 121</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Oth. 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Dom. 10 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
